货币战争
A currency war is an escalation of currency devaluation policies among two or more nations. Nations devalue their currencies in order to make their own exports more attactive in markets abroad. At the same time, such devaluation makes imports more expensive to the nation's own consumers, forcing them to choose home-grown subsitutes. This combination of export-let growth and increased domestic demand usually contributes to higher employment and faster economic growth. Economists view currency wars as harmful to the gobal economy because these bach-and-forth actions by nations seeking a competitive advantage could have unforeseen adverse consequences, such as increased protectionism and trade barriers